---
description: Standardize domain type and model definitions in shared/types.
globs: src/shared/types/**/*.ts
alwaysApply: false
---

# Types and Models

- Domain-level models live in `src/shared/types` as `*.types.ts` files (e.g. `event.types.ts`, `filter.types.ts`) and are re-exported from the `index.ts` barrel – follow this pattern for new domains.
- Use PascalCase for interfaces and types, and keep names explicit (`Event`, `EventStatus`, `FilterOptions` etc.) instead of vague catch-all names.
- If you find yourself copying or slightly tweaking an existing shared type, pause and either reuse or extend it; do not spam near-duplicate types.
- Avoid embedding complex anonymous object types inline in many places – promote them into named types in `shared/types` when they are reused or important.
- When a type is truly feature-specific and not shared, keep it close to the feature, but move it into `shared/types` the moment it crosses feature boundaries.
